course: dictionary
lesson: 8999
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them as numbered senses. Skeleton can mean the bones inside a body, a model of those bones, or the main frame of something. Context tells you which meaning is right. «Many dinosaur skeletons are casts, copies made from moulds» means a model, because copies and moulds are the clues.
explain: «A tortoise's shell is part of its skeleton, joined to its ribs and backbone, so it can never leave it.» Here skeleton means the frame of bones that supports and protects the body. Ribs and backbone are the clues.
explain: Phrases carry their own meanings. A skeleton staff is the smallest number of people needed to keep something running, and a skeleton in the cupboard is an embarrassing secret. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. If it still makes sense, you have found the right sense.
fact: A skeleton is the frame of bones that supports and protects the body.
fact: In science, the skeleton has three main jobs: support, protection and movement.
fact: An adult human has 206 bones; babies have more, and some of them later join together.
fact: Some animals have skeletons made of cartilage, the bendy stuff in your ear, not bone. Spotted eagle rays are one example.
fact: Skeleton can also mean a model of bones, or the main frame of a building or a story plan.
exercise: «Many dinosaur skeletons are casts, copies made from moulds.» In this sentence, skeleton means | A cupboard full of secrets | The bones inside a living body | *A copy or model of the bones | A small team of workers
exercise: «A tortoise's shell is part of its skeleton, joined to its ribs and backbone.» What does skeleton mean here? | A model made of plastic | *The frame of bones that supports and protects the body | The smallest team needed for a job | The main story of a film
exercise: Which phrase means the smallest number of people needed to keep something running? | *Skeleton staff | Skeleton in the cupboard | Human skeleton | Dinosaur skeleton
test: «Cleaning one big skeleton out of hard rock can take years of patient work.» Which meaning of skeleton fits best? | *Real fossil bones, still inside hard rock | A secret hidden in a cupboard | A plan for a story | A team of workers
test: «Spotted eagle rays have skeletons of cartilage, not bone.» What is cartilage? | Hard shell | *The bendy stuff in your ear | Bones of a fish | Muscle
exam: In «A skeleton in the cupboard is an embarrassing secret», what does skeleton mean? | A pile of old bones | The main frame of a house | A team that works hard | *An embarrassing secret
